-- title:
--   Inertia at a Taylor–Wiles prime acts as χ⊕χ⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative noetherian local ring that is complete with respect to the adic topology of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$, and let $\rho$ be an object of [`GaloisRepAdic R`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16): a finite free $R$-module $V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (the $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) to $\mathrm{End}_R V$ which is $\mathfrak m$-adically continuous, in the sense that for each $n$ there is a finite subextension $L/\mathbb Q$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\rho(\sigma)v-v\in\mathfrak m^n V$ for all $v$ whenever $\sigma$ fixes $L$ pointwise. Let $p$ be a prime and assume `ρ.DetIsCyclotomic p`: $p\in\mathfrak m$, and for all $n$, all $\sigma$ and all $a\in\mathbb N$, if $\sigma\mu=\mu^a$ for every $p^n$-th root of unity $\mu$, then $\det\rho(\sigma)-a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq p$ and $p\mid q-1$. Assume that the residual representation $\bar\rho$ on $\mathrm{ResidueField}(R)\otimes_R V$ is unramified at $q$, i.e. $\bar\rho(\sigma)=1$ for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ in its non-units and every $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$; and assume regularity of residual Frobenius: for every such $P$ and every $\varphi$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and inducing $x\mapsto x^q$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\varphi)$ equals $(X-\alpha)(X-\beta)$ for some $\alpha\neq\beta$ in the residue field of $R$. Let $k$ be a natural number with $p^{k+1}\nmid q-1$, let $\mathrm{cyc}:\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ be a monoid homomorphism satisfying $\sigma\mu=\mu^{\mathrm{cyc}(\sigma)}$ for all $q$-th roots of unity $\mu$, and let $\pi_\Delta:(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\to\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/p^k)$ be a surjective monoid homomorphism. Then there is a monoid homomorphism $\chi:\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/p^k)\to R^\times$ such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ among its non-units there is an $R$-basis $b_0,b_1$ of $V$ with $\rho(\sigma)b_0=\chi(\pi_\Delta(\mathrm{cyc}\,\sigma))\,b_0$ and $\rho(\sigma)b_1=\chi(\pi_\Delta(\mathrm{cyc}\,\sigma))^{-1}b_1$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia group at $P$. The character $\chi$ is uniform in $P$, while the basis is allowed to depend on $P$.
--
--   This is the description of the local structure of a lift at a Taylor–Wiles prime $q$ (Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, Lemma 2.44): inertia at $q$ acts diagonally through a character of the $p$-part of $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ and its inverse. It is used in the construction of the patching data and of the presentations of the local Hecke algebras in the Taylor–Wiles argument.
